# video_framectl_one_fence.sby — VIDEO.FRAMECTL formal properties (plan
# W2.2 §4; spec/video_rules.md §8: exactly one completion fence per
# displayed frame, tick rate one per frame period, reset-idle).
#
# The raster is ABSTRACTED in the harness (a small-period vswap_dec /
# frame_start generator with the same ordering law as the real raster:
# frame_start follows each dec). slot_ready / deadline_cycles are FREE
# (adversarial flapping included); the DUT's free-running counters are
# assumption-bounded to a 32-frame window (documented in the harness — the
# unbounded counters are exercised by the random lanes). The two clock
# domains are TIED (gpu_clk = vid_clk): the toggle+2FF crossing degenerates
# to a fixed delay and the fence-count law is unaffected.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required (ledger rule V16):
#   bmc   — the counting laws hold over a 60-step window (~4 abstract frame
#           periods). An UNBOUNDED abc-pdr prove of the same assertions was
#           observed to complete green ONCE (2026-08-16, ~2,600 CPU-s,
#           logfile in the run records) but its runtime is far past the
#           lane's 1800 s wrapper budget and varies run-to-run — a lane
#           task that only sometimes finishes is a flaky-green, so the
#           RECORDED task is the bounded one and the pdr pass is a note,
#           not a badge. (Cost driver: pdr digging invariants out of the
#           64-bit counter registers; the harness already bounds their
#           reachable values but not their widths.)
#   cover — fence / tick / repeat / commit-swap / two-frame antecedents all
#           reachable (the salvaged harness had NO covers).
#
# Run via `ctest -L formal` (shared hardened wrapper) or by hand:
#   sby -f --prefix <workdir> video_framectl_one_fence.sby

[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 60
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 40
expect pass

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
plugin -i slang
read_slang --top video_framectl_fv -DFORMAL zhao_abi_pkg.sv zhao_pkg.sv zhao_video_framectl.sv video_framectl_fv.sv
prep -top video_framectl_fv

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/generated/zhao_abi_pkg.sv
../../fpga/rtl/common/zhao_pkg.sv
../../fpga/rtl/video/zhao_video_framectl.sv
video_framectl_fv.sv
